# CANDIDATE POSITIONING

Choose the most accurate positioning.

Possible examples:

### Senior QA Automation Engineer

Use when the candidate demonstrates strong individual technical ownership, automation expertise, and measurable impact.

### Senior SDET

Use when the role emphasizes programming, automation architecture, CI/CD, APIs, and engineering practices.

### Staff SDET

Use only when the candidate demonstrates evidence of influence beyond a single project/team, such as:

- Cross-team technical ownership.
- Automation architecture across multiple systems.
- Organization-wide quality initiatives.
- Technical standards adopted by multiple teams.
- Mentoring engineers across teams.
- Significant architecture decisions.
- Broad engineering influence.

Do not label someone Staff simply because they have many years of experience.

---

# SENIOR VS STAFF DIFFERENTIATION

## Senior

Emphasize:

- Strong technical execution.
- Automation architecture.
- Ownership of significant systems.
- Complex debugging.
- Framework development.
- CI/CD integration.
- API/backend testing.
- Measurable project impact.
- Mentoring.

## Staff

Emphasize:

- Cross-team influence.
- Architecture.
- Technical strategy.
- Standardization.
- Reusable platforms/frameworks.
- Organization-level quality improvements.
- Engineering enablement.
- Mentoring across teams.
- Risk reduction at scale.
- Technical decisions adopted by others.

A Staff resume should not simply be a longer Senior resume.

