# DO NOT TURN THE RESUME INTO A TECHNOLOGY LIST

A Senior SDET resume should not read like:

> Java | Python | Selenium | Playwright | Postman | Jenkins | Docker | AWS | SQL | Jira | Git | Linux | REST | API | Appium...

Technology lists are supporting evidence.

Experience bullets must demonstrate how the technologies were used to solve engineering problems.

---

# ATS OPTIMIZATION

Use exact JD terminology when accurate.

For example:

If the JD says:

**"End-to-end testing using Playwright and TypeScript"**

and the candidate actually has that experience, prefer:

**"End-to-end test automation using Playwright and TypeScript"**

rather than:

**"Automated browser testing using a modern web testing framework."**

Do not replace accurate terminology with generic synonyms.

Do not repeat the same keyword unnaturally.

---

# RESUME LENGTH

For Senior SDET:

**One page is preferred when the candidate has enough relevant experience to present clearly within one page.**

For Staff SDET or candidates with 10+ years of relevant experience:

**Two pages may be appropriate when necessary to demonstrate significant technical scope and leadership.**

Never remove important evidence solely to meet an arbitrary page limit.

Never use two pages simply because the candidate has a long employment history.

---

# FORMATTING

Use:

- Single column.
- ATS-friendly structure.
- Clear section headings.
- Consistent dates.
- Consistent typography.
- Short bullets.
- Strong visual hierarchy.
- Minimal decoration.

Avoid:

- Skill bars.
- Stars.
- Graphs.
- Large icons.
- Photos.
- Tables containing critical information.
- Dense paragraphs.
- Excessive colors.
- Multi-column layouts.

---

# LINKS

Use clickable links for:

- LinkedIn
- GitHub
- Portfolio
- Technical blog

Never display long raw URLs.

Remove broken links.

---

# PERSONAL INFORMATION

Do not include:

- Photo
- Age
- Date of birth
- Gender
- Religion
- Marital status
- Full postal address
- Personal ID numbers

Include location and work authorization only when relevant to the target market/application.

